# Data files
# Unanchored, so this matches a `data/` directory at any depth beneath
# cognisom/ -- including packaged reference data, not just runtime output.
data/
# Reference proteome: versioned package data, regenerated by
# scripts/fetch_reference_proteome.py. Must be tracked, or an installed
# package silently falls back to a per-gene UniProt fetch at runtime.
!genomics/data/
!genomics/data/**
# ...except the MANE Select proteome, which is ~6 MB of derived data rebuilt
# by scripts/fetch_mane_proteome.py. The curated FASTA above is small and
# authored, so it is tracked; this one is large and regenerable, so it is not.
# This rule must come after the negations above, or they would re-include it.
genomics/data/mane_select_proteins.faa.gz
*.csv
*.tsv

# Tissue-section fixtures: packaged test input, not runtime output. A few
# tens of KB of measured cell positions that tissue_section.py loads, so
# they must be tracked or the section layout raises FileNotFoundError on
# a fresh clone and every test of it errors.
#
# LAST IN THE FILE ON PURPOSE, for the same reason the MANE rule above is
# placed after its negations: later rules win, and both `data/` and the
# blanket `*.csv` would otherwise re-exclude these. Git also does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so re-including a file inside
# `data/` needs that directory un-excluded at EVERY level -- a lone
# `!/data/sections/**` silently matches nothing. Anchored with a leading
# slash so this reaches only cognisom/data/ and leaves a `data/`
# directory at any other depth excluded as before.
!/data/
/data/*
!/data/sections/
!/data/sections/**
